executionContract.intendedBehavior:
On a Windows host, storedProfile also reads the persisted profile pin when the IDE state store root or the project base has no physical folder, that is when physicalFolder(path) == null:
- no drive mapping can place it, as written or through a junction, link or subst expansion (for example \Device\ImDisk0, or a null or throwing windowsDriveTarget);
- the real path of an existing folder cannot be found;
- it is spelled without a drive.
52fb6178's plain-base terms stay.
Such a store or base is unprovable, not inside. A stored PROTECTED pin keeps profile() PROTECTED and requests the downgrade confirmation, and a confirmed downgrade writes nothing.
These still behave as before:
- a provably-outside store is read and written as before;
- a store proved inside on a placed drive (the runIde sandbox, D2) reads ABSENT;
- a missing base reads ABSENT.
physicalFolder is extracted from outsideByIdentity unchanged, so no selection answer changes.
